1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,160
Right now, there's a hole in
your vision,

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:03,500
and you can't see it.

3
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:07,040
At the back of each eye, the
optic nerve exits through

4
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:08,710
one small patch of the retina.

5
00:00:09,125 --> 00:00:11,385
That patch has no light sensors
at all.

6
00:00:12,005 --> 00:00:13,645
Light landing there is never
detected.

7
00:00:14,125 --> 00:00:17,485
It's called the blind spot, and
every human eye has one.

8
00:00:17,833 --> 00:00:19,273
So why don't you notice a gap?

9
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:23,223
With both eyes open, each eye
fills in what the other

10
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:24,033
one misses.

11
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:27,600
And even with one eye shut, your
brain doesn't show you a

12
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:28,240
hole.

13
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:29,040
Try it.

14
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:31,550
Close your left eye and stare
straight ahead with your right.

15
00:00:31,917 --> 00:00:35,067
Hold a fingertip in front of
you, and slowly move it to the

16
00:00:35,077 --> 00:00:35,877
right.

17
00:00:35,957 --> 00:00:37,637
At one point, the tip vanishes.

18
00:00:38,083 --> 00:00:39,343
That's your blind spot.

19
00:00:39,783 --> 00:00:40,923
It's been there all along.
